I wrote the hidden suite: 69 tests in four files under `packages/db/test/hidden-trim-hyphens/`. It compiles with `tsc -p tsconfig.test.json` with no errors. Every test currently **passes**, which breaks your rule that each test must fail against the seam as it stands.

**Why they pass:** `packages/db/src/emails.ts` has no `not implemented` bodies. `toHandleBase` still has the original regex strip, `replace(/^-+|-+$/g, "")`. The spec requires the output to stay exactly the same as that regex version for every input, so the current code is the reference. A correct test has to pass against it. I didn't change the seam; to get the "fails first" check, the `toHandleBase` body needs to be replaced with a throwing stub.

**Slow cases:** on the current regex code, the long interior-run tests take about 3.4 s each, and the 200,000-hyphen one takes about 13.7 s. That is the quadratic cost the spec describes. A linear implementation should run them in milliseconds. None of them checks timing, because the spec says not to.

**What the suite covers:**
- **Every scenario:** each of the 19 scenario keys (happy 1–4, boundary 1–10, unhappy 1–3, concurrency 1) has a test that runs all its outline examples.
- **Extensions:** each public test has at least one extension, named in a comment above it. They use other run lengths, unequal or longer edge runs, more items, other orders and separate stores.
- **Tuned shortcuts:** these are the wrong implementations the suite is built to catch:
  - stripping only a fixed number of hyphens;
  - collapsing interior runs into one hyphen;
  - trimming underscores or any non-alphanumeric character;
  - truncating before trimming (for example, 25 `x`, 10 hyphens, then `b` must give 25 `x` and 5 hyphens);
  - trimming again after the cut;
  - capping the local part's length to bound the work (300,000 leading hyphens before `dana`);
  - doing the replacement before lowercasing (the Kelvin sign `K` must give `kelvin`);
  - off-by-one errors at the ends of the index walk;
  - keeping state or caching between calls (repeated and interleaved inputs of the same length).
- **Collisions:** the counter and the random fallback are checked on padded stems (`jo-user`), the `-user` stem, and stems trimmed from 100,000-hyphen runs.

69 tests, in 4 files.

Open in the spec: none
